  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;be defined as,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>cot</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;is continuous at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to:</p>"
